Z||000000||Carrolles||01-12-2000||06:50 AM||||I was at Gibbs Auto yesterday in Augusta, GA ((706) 722-8571) and saw a newly arrived 88 coupe with right front damage.  The fender is smashed and the right front rim is bent. and the windshield is cracked.  I couldn't tell if there is any suspension damage.  Other than that the car looks good.  It is very clean and even smells nice inside.<P>It is a black basic coupe without many options.<P>They said they'd sell the whole car for $850.00.  I'm not interested in it myself.  They haven't inventoried it yet.  It probably won't last long once they do.<P>There is also an 88 T-top coupe in another yard (Craven Auto ((706) 790-6365) in Augusta, GA that has been pretty well picked over.  The windshield is smashed and the driver side windshield post is bent slightly.  The T-top frame is intack and the seals don't look too bad.  The t-tops are missing.  They won't sell the entire car but will sell parts.  It looks like all of the suspension is there but the engine and trans and shifter are gone.||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||01-11-2000||10:07 PM||||I've found an 88 Coupe in running condition, 4 cylinder with an auto, damaged nose and tail for $575 or best offer. Looks like it's been abused. Thinking about offering $400 for it. Might be a good SCCA race car project.||||reg||1
